<td id="A2.T6.5.1.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A2.T6.5.1.7.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">20.42</span></td>
<td id="A2.T6.5.1.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A2.T6.5.1.7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">17.91</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Generated Videos from SV4D 2.0</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We previously noted that the quality of generated multi-view frames from SV4D 2.0 decays over time.
Figure <a href="#A2.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ B.2 Generated Videos from SV4D 2.0 ‣ Appendix B More Results ‣ WildSmoke: Ready-to-Use Dynamic 3D Smoke Assetsfrom a Single Video in the Wild" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> shows early and late frames of the sequence. As time progresses, the smoke structure gradually collapses.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.11114v1/sv4d_sample.png" id="A2.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/363;" width="685" height="363" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F12.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="A2.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">SV4D 2.0 multi-view generation over time. Later frames exhibit structural collapse.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>SSIM and LPIPS</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond PSNR, we further report the structural similarity index measure (SSIM) in Table <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ B.3 SSIM and LPIPS ‣ Appendix B More Results ‣ WildSmoke: Ready-to-Use Dynamic 3D Smoke Assetsfrom a Single Video in the Wild" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and the perceptual metric LPIPS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite> in Table <a href="#A2.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ B.3 SSIM and LPIPS ‣ Appendix B More Results ‣ WildSmoke: Ready-to-Use Dynamic 3D Smoke Assetsfrom a Single Video in the Wild" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. Our method is still shown to perform better based on these two additional metrics.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 7</span>: </span><span id="A2.T7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparing SSIM (higher is better) of smoke reconstruction by different methods on videos collected from FLAME <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite> and <a href="https://pixabay.com/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href ltx_framed ltx_framed_underline" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;">Pixabay</a>.
</span></figcaption>
<div id="A2.T7.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:188.8pt;height:31.3pt;vertical-align:-14.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-90.1pt,14.9pt) scale(0.511754989367412,0.511754989367412) ;">
